title:: CaosInstrument
summary:: A track voice: SynthDef or function, route, params and note line.
categories:: CaosBox
related:: Classes/CaosGear, Classes/CaosTrack

description::
A CaosInstrument knows how to sound (SynthDef or function), where it goes out
(code::out::), with which parameters (code::params::) and, if melodic, how its
note line advances. It does not know about the GUI or the clock: it receives
code::trigger::, code::set::, code::release:: and code::free::.

list::
## code::kind:: — code::\synth:: or code::\function::.
## code::mode:: — code::\free:: advances with the clock; code::\trig:: advances on trigger.
## code::retrigger:: — a new voice per trigger, or legato.
## code::oneShot:: — percussive envelopes with no live node to release.
::

instancemethods::

method:: trigger
method:: set
method:: out
code::
i = CaosGear.new.bass(50);
i.out_(\master);
i.set(\cutf, 1200);
i.trigger;
i.release;
::
